        "notes": "ROUND 7\nPowers: Strangle Step and Revolving Ruin are both good - I personally prefer Strangle Step for more mobility and a quicker escape if necessary. Also, high WP means more lifesteal, so it pairs nicely with Strangle Step.\n\nAt this point, you've reached round 7 for a few potential reasons:\n-If you're dying a lot: Stop peeking the enemy DPS and only engage when you can get on top of them. If that fails, play with your tank and look for kills in the brawl.\n\n-If the enemy D.Va is dominating/unkillable: She probably picked survival percs and has around 1300hp. If this is the case, tell your teammates to pick Codebreaker + Volskaya Ordnance if they can, as this power works well on tanks with 1000+ hp. \n\n-If your other DPS is struggling: Try to put as much pressure on the enemy backline as you can to draw attention and give your DPS time to stay alive. Getting picks by flanking can win fights, especially if the enemy team doesn't have a Mercy.\n\n-If your supports are getting killed by enemy divers: Play to react to dives and pressure them off when they try to go for your supports.\n\nIn general, in round 7 you want at least 70% WP to punch through targets with high health and healing, but try to go for targets you are sure you can defeat in a duel. Remember to teleport and move around a lot to remain unpredictable, as this is important, especially in the last round.",
